            {'cat': 'wildlife', 'q': 'Why are African Fish Eagle calls so famous on Lake Naivasha?', 'a': 'The African Fish Eagle’s haunting, evocative call is known as the "Voice of Africa." Lake Naivasha boasts one of the highest densities of nesting fish eagles in the world, allowing travelers to hear their ringing calls across calm waters. Paradise Boat Rides delivers transparent, budget-friendly pricing with zero hidden fees, experienced local captains, certified life.'},
            {'cat': 'wildlife', 'q': 'Are flamingos present on Lake Naivasha?', 'a': 'Flamingos prefer alkaline salt lakes like Nakuru or Bogoria. However, nearby Lake Oloiden (connected to Naivasha) occasionally hosts thousands of lesser flamingos when blue-green algae blooms occur. Paradise Boat Rides delivers transparent, budget-friendly pricing with zero hidden fees, experienced local captains, certified life jackets, and direct WhatsApp booking for an unforgettable Lake Naivasha safari.'},
            {'cat': 'wildlife', 'q': 'What aquatic vegetation grows in Lake Naivasha?', 'a': 'The lake is famous for dense floating papyrus fringing (Cyperus papyrus), water hyacinth, and submerged macrophyte beds. These plants filter lake water, provide nursery habitat for fish, and shelter waterfowl. Paradise Boat Rides delivers transparent, budget-friendly pricing with zero hidden fees, experienced local captains, certified life jackets, and direct WhatsApp booking for an unforgettable Lake Naivasha safari.'},
