            {'cat': 'wildlife', 'q': 'How do hippos spend their time in Lake Naivasha?', 'a': 'Hippos spend 16 hours a day resting in shallow water to protect sensitive skin from equatorial sun. At night, they emerge onto grassy shores, traveling up to 10 km inland to consume up to 40 kg of grass before returning at dawn.'},
